  ],
  "description": "June 1981 first-edition engaged effect circuit. MN3005 and clock use a sampled-charge model, combined outputs and a calibrated timing network. The NE570 uses analog feedback compression and feedforward expansion with matched full-wave envelope detectors with a small idle floor. The bypass latch and clock feedthrough are omitted. The op-amps use 1 V nominal headroom from both ends of the 9 V supply.",
  "io": {
    "groundNode": "0",
    "inputNode": "in",
    "outputNode": "out"
  },
